From 621b3a8d6ad1a4283e35b534ee66b391b883cdf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch <patch@local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 17:54:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let owners re-pin a photo that already has a location

The permission rule in PATCH /api/photos/location has always allowed an
owner to move their own photo (`or(ownerId = me, lat IS NULL)`), but the
UI never offered the affordance. PlacePicker is the only entry into the
map's pick mode, it is rendered only when `unplaced.length > 0`, and it
lists `unplaced` photos exclusively. The moment a photo gets coordinates
it leaves that list, so a hand-placed pin was final for everyone --
including the person who placed it, and including a wrong EXIF fix.

Adds an owner-only control to the lightbox that hands the photo back to
the map's existing pick mode. No new API surface and no schema change.

Also rolls the optimistic update back per-id against the server's
`updated` list instead of the HTTP status. The route skips rows the
permission rule excludes rather than failing, so it answers 200 with a
short list; the old code treated that as success and left a pin on
screen the server never stored. PlaceBoard already trusted `updated`
this way -- the map page now matches.
---
 src/app/(app)/page.tsx      | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 src/components/Lightbox.tsx | 67 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 97 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

